  "notes": "Historical year 2025-2026. Pattern B companion file to PSYCHBA-2025.json. The B.S. at Brandywine offered both Business and Science options; this historical file represents the Business Option as published in the 2025-2026 bulletin archive. Scraper output (ok:true, archive URL: bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/undergraduate/colleges/university-college/psychology-bs/) shows the Business Option plan continuing in this year's archive. All course codes used here come from the scraper's 'linked_codes' field (PSYCH 100, ENGL 15, ENGL 30H, PSYCH 301W, ENGL 202A). No unverified codes flagged in this year's run. Total credits per bulletin: 116-119. This is the final year before the 2026-2027 live bulletin, which shifted the featured plan to the Science Option (see PSYCHBSBW-2026.json). Entrance to major requires 2.0 GPA, per the 2025-2026 bulletin archive. QA FIX (2025-09-18, reviewer #2): the scraper correctly reported the bulletin's \"PSYCH 200 or STAT 200\" plan-grid cell as un-hyperlinked (is_generic_slot=True) for this program/year, but the label unambiguously names two real, catalog-verified courses -- it was originally modeled as a generic slot (only a text label, no options), which meant build_full_plan never actually enrolled the student in either course, so PSYCH 301W (whose real prereq is PSYCH 100 AND (PSYCH 200 or STAT 200)) could never schedule. Fixed to type=course with options [\"PSYCH 200\",\"STAT 200\"], matching how the pre-existing PSYCHBSBW-2026.json already models this same requirement. That fix then surfaced a second, real, previously-masked gap: PSYCH 200 itself also requires MATH 21 (prereq_groups AND-of-ORs: PSYCH 100 AND MATH 21) per catalogs/psych_catalog.json, which this bulletin's suggested-plan table never lists -- added MATH 21 as a bolt-on Semester 1 course item (same placement-gate convention already used in BUSINESS/ETI/HCDD/PSYCHBABW-2022..2025), bumping Semester 1 target_credits from 13.5 to 16.5. Re-ran build_full_plan(star